  "id": "neurolinguistics",
  "term": "neurolinguistics",
  "definition": "Neurolinguistics is the study of how brain processes are involved in language and language development. In this context, it views language growth as an active, embodied process shaped by interaction, feedback, and multimodal engagement rather than by input alone.",
